-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Nov  1 19:16:00 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- New package: TextureCraft 0.2.0 (upstream tag v0.2.0,
  2026-11-01), a 3D texture painter in pure Rust, plus the
  texturecraft-cli command line, MCP and JSON-lines server:
  * Vendored with update=false against the upstream lockfile into
    vendor-texturecraft.tar.zst (a cargo_vendor tag, as upstream's
    own vendor/ holds its patched egui-phosphor)
  * Vendor audit: licence re-derived over the two shipped targets
    (see the spec notice), including LGPL-2.1-or-later for the KDE
    blur protocol bindings winit links; zip 2.4.2 has
    RUSTSEC-2026-0367, RUSTSEC-2026-0368 and RUSTSEC-2026-0369, all
    in extract(), which texturecraft never calls (archive entries
    are read into memory), and only the incompatible zip 9 fixes
    them, so nothing is pinned
  * No self-updater, download, telemetry or plugin loading; the MCP
    and JSON-lines servers and the app's control channel are opt-in
    and loopback-only
  * texturecraft-control-token-0600.patch: write the --control
    token owner-only (0600), like the CLI does
  * Ship the MIT licence text of the embedded Phosphor icon font
    (LICENSE-phosphor.txt, from phosphor-icons/web v2.1.1)

